<title>SRI LANKA: Ceylon Grains falls on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Ceylon Grains falls on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ceylon grain Elevators Ltd fell 3.45 percent, or 50 cents, to 14 rupees, on selling of 10,300 shares, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;A retail investor who bought the share at around 12.50, is taking profit,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>The company is a feed miller and breeder of day-old chicks. It is a unit of Prima Ltd of Singapore.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
